## Findings and supporting checks

1. Public input/result types use borrowed strings with explicit lifetimes and
   small `Copy` enums. The result borrows the captured strings rather than the
   wrapper's lifetime. Internal, display, holder-group and sort identities stay
   distinct. The pure resolver introduces no I/O, unsafe code, allocation,
   dependency, async state, model mutation, or existing DTO field change.
2. `Unavailable` produces a typed error implementing standard `Display` and
   `Error`; it cannot silently become non-Gradle or a reported-null getter.
   `Option<&str>` is documented as a reported-null value. Standard suffix
   operations avoid unchecked indexing and production panics. `unwrap_or` here
   is an infallible optional-label fallback, not an unchecked unwrap.
3. Comments and rustdoc explain non-obvious fidelity boundaries: raw path
   equality, observed nulls, imported/collision names, holder capture, empty
   labels and separate Kotlin facts. The API is a distinct logical component
   within the existing crate, matching repository layout conventions.
4. All 20 test declarations match both provenance and task-port inventories.
   Tests assert source-derived observable cases covering non-Gradle/unavailable,
   source-set precedence, root/nonroot and missing IDs, null/empty distinction,
   colon suffixes, raw/case-sensitive paths, Unicode/whitespace, separate
   identities, holder fallback, and borrowed long names. No `ignore`, conditional
   exclusion, expected-panic shortcut, or existing-test modification was found.
   These are supplemental policy tests; they are not claimed as original ports.
5. Independently verified the 159-path original-preservation inventory against
   base Git bytes. 158 paths are byte-identical; the remaining path is exactly
   the one additive `pub mod module_presentation;` export in `android_tools.rs`.
   Existing crate metadata/build scripts, public DTOs, fixtures, canonical
   reference manifest and parity matrix are preserved.
6. All eight full reference source files match their declared sizes/SHA-256
   values and independent local reference copies. Original Apache headers are
   present. `LICENSE-APACHE` is byte-identical to the retained Apache 2.0 license
   (SHA-256 `cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`).
   NOTICE retains AOSP/JetBrains attribution and explicitly states zero original
   ports; the Rust policy/tests retain the relevant AOSP attribution.
7. Task documentation and port/provenance JSON accurately retain zero original
   test credit, `not_run`/pending runtime status, and incomplete original tree,
   phase and IDE flags. They explicitly leave authoritative identity producers,
   holder lookup, Kotlin facet import, revision publication, empty-label adapter
   support, project-panel wiring and original generated-tree workflows unported.
   The task notes do not claim UI or full-app fidelity. The docs automation
   instructions' `docs/src/` scope does not require an unrelated mdBook rewrite
   for these task records under `docs/android-studio/`.

## Execution limits

Read `.rules`, `docs/AGENTS.md` and `docs/.rules`. Per the assigned review scope,
ran only read-only file/Git inspection and Python JSON/hash verification, plus
`git diff --check` on the additive export (passed). No Cargo, Gradle, compiler,
app, formatter or cache command was run, and no source, fixture, matrix, branch
or protected repository state was changed. The task owner must still obtain
actual normal locked all-feature tests, library build, repository `./script/clippy`
and formatting results; Root must run the subsequent combined full app/live and
full-workspace gates before protected merge.

An initial reviewer inventory assertion incorrectly equated the 157 original
paths included in the frozen source closure with the full 159-path preservation
inventory. The two canonical metadata JSON paths are in the latter inventory;
the corrected independent check verified both all 159 baseline paths and all
172 frozen current paths. This was a reviewer audit setup error, not a product
finding or source change. The note is retained in the verification receipt.

